    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/0809.0975v2</id>
    <title>Production of the neutral top-pion $π_{t}^{0}$ in association with a high-$p_{T}$ jet at the $LHC$</title>
    <updated>2008-12-06T02:53:03Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/0809.0975v2" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/0809.0975v2" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>  In the framework of the topcolor-assisted technicolor $(TC2)$ model, we study production of the neutral top-pion $π_{t}^{0}$ in association with a high-$p_{T}$ jet at the $LHC$, which proceeds via the partonic processes $gg\longrightarrow π_{t}^{0}g$, $gq\longrightarrow π_{t}^{0}q$, $q\bar{q}\longrightarrow π_{t}^{0}g$, $gb(\bar{b})\longrightarrow π_{t}^{0}b(\bar{b})$, and $b\bar{b}\longrightarrow π_{t}^{0}g$. We find that it is very challenging to detect the neutral top-pion $π_{t}^{0}$ via the process $pp\longrightarrow π_{t}^{0}+jet+X\to t\bar{t}+jet+X$, while the possible signatures of $π_{t}^{0}$ might be detected via the process $pp\longrightarrow π_{t}^{0}+jet+X\to(\bar{t}c+t\bar{c})+jet+X$ at the $LHC$.</summary>
    <category term="hep-ph" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
    <published>2008-09-05T08:28:57Z</published>
    <arxiv:comment>13 pages, 4 figures; typos corrected</arxiv:comment>
    <arxiv:primary_category term="hep-ph"/>
