  <entry>
    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-ph/0402212v1</id>
    <title>Determining the ratio of the H^+ -&gt; τνto H^+ -&gt; t b-bar decay rates for large \tanβat the Large Hadron Collider</title>
    <updated>2004-02-19T17:52:56Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-ph/0402212v1" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/hep-ph/0402212v1" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>  We present results on the determination of the observable ratio R=BR(H^+ -&gt; τν)/BR(H^+ -&gt; t b-bar) of charged Higgs boson decay rates as a discriminant quantity between Supersymmetric and non-Supersymmetric models. Simulation of measurements of this quantity through the analysis of the charged Higgs production process gb-&gt; t b H^+ and relative backgrounds in the two above decay channels has been performed in the context of ATLAS. A ~12-14% accuracy on R can be achieved for \tanβ=50, \mHc=300-500 GeV and after an integrated luminosity of 300 fb^-1. With this precision measurement, the Large Hadron Collider (LHC) can easily discriminate between models for the two above scenarios, so long as \tanβ&gt; 20.</summary>
    <category term="hep-ph" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
    <published>2004-02-19T17:52:56Z</published>
